---
description: Prefer single dashes over emdashes in markdown and comments
alwaysApply: true
---

# Dash Style (No Emdash)

Do not use the emdash character (`—`) in markdown or code comments.

- Use a single hyphen/dash (`-`) instead of an emdash.
- Exception: for a mid-sentence subclause, use a pair of dashes with spaces: ` -- like this -- `.

```markdown
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
Updated sorting — now respects priority markers.

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
Updated sorting - now respects priority markers.

<!-- ✅ GOOD (subclause) -->
The filter -- when enabled -- hides completed items.
```
